---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../config';
---

<Base title="Submit a compatibility report — SharpEmu">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 pt-12" data-pagefind-body>
    <PageHeader title="Submit a compatibility report">
      Two ways to contribute, easiest first.
    </PageHeader>
    <div class="prose prose-slate dark:prose-invert mt-10 max-w-none">
    <h2>1. Open an issue</h2>
    <p>
      Use the{" "}
      <a href={`${SITE.siteRepoUrl}/issues/new?template=compatibility_report.yml`}>
        compatibility report template</a
      >. A maintainer will convert it into a report page.
    </p>
    <h2>2. Open a pull request</h2>
    <p>
      Add a markdown file at <code>src/content/compat/&lt;os&gt;/&lt;TITLEID&gt;.md</code>, where{' '}
      <code>&lt;os&gt;</code> is <code>windows</code>, <code>linux</code> or <code>macos</code> (e.g.{' '}
      <code>windows/PPSA01284.md</code>). PS5 games use their <code>PPSA</code> title ID and PS4 games their{' '}
      <code>CUSA</code> one; a game's PS4 and PS5 versions get separate reports.
    </p>
    <pre><code>---
titleId: PPSA01284   # PPSAxxxxx for PS5, CUSAxxxxx for PS4
status: ingame        # nothing | boots | menus | ingame | playable
testedVersion: dev    # SharpEmu release or commit (sharpemu-mac on macOS)
testedDate: 2026-07-17
gameVersion: "1.004"  # optional game update/version
os: windows           # windows | linux | macos — must match the folder
hardware: "RTX 4070, Ryzen 5 7600"
score: 3              # optional 1-5 experience rating
---

What works, what breaks, workarounds. Screenshots welcome —
put images next to the file and reference them relatively.</code></pre>
    <h2>Ground rules</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Test with dumps of games you own. Piracy reports are removed.</li>
      <li>One report per game per OS — update the existing file if it's outdated.</li>
      <li>
        Note the exact SharpEmu build you tested. On macOS that's a build of{' '}
        <a href={SITE.macRepoUrl}>sharpemu-mac</a>; Windows and Linux builds come from{' '}
        <a href={SITE.repoUrl}>sharpemu</a>.
      </li>
      <li>Maintainers can add the <code>compat-approved</code> label to create a validated PR automatically.</li>
    </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
